===Etymology 2===
A noun of the adjectival form {{m|is|svangur||hungry; thin}}. Compare the {{der|is|non|svangi||the groins, especially of animals}} which was also spelled {{m|non|svangr||the groins, especially of animals}}.

{{wikipedia|lang=is}}
{{wikipedia|magi|lang=is}}

====Noun====
{{is-noun|m|svangs|svangar}}

# an [[empty]] or [[hungry]] [[stomach]]; used in set phrases
#: ''Ég held að ég [[fá sér í svanginn|fái mér eitthvað í '''svanginn''']].''
#:: I think I'll get something to eat.

=====Usage notes=====
* In modern Icelandic, this word is predominantly used in the [[accusative case]] with a [[definite article]] ("[[svanginn]]") in the set phrase {{m|is|fá sér í svanginn|fá sér eitthvað í svanginn|to get something to eat}}.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|fá sér í svanginn}} (to get something to eat)

